# Flutter Development

## Stack

- Use **Flutter** (stable channel) and **Dart 3+** with sound null safety
- Targets are **Android (phones and tablets)** and **web** only; the app lives in `flutter_app/`
- Use **Material 3** widgets and theming (`ThemeData`, `ColorScheme`); no hard-coded colors or text styles in widgets outside the theme
- The legacy vanilla web app was removed; consult git history if original behavior needs checking

## Architecture

- Layered structure under `lib/`: `core/` (pure Dart logic), `models/`, `state/` (controllers), `services/` (I/O), `ui/` (widgets and screens)
- Keep `core/` free of Flutter imports so it is unit-testable
- State management with **provider** and `ChangeNotifier` controllers; widgets stay thin
- Persisted JSON keeps the legacy field names (`version: 1`, schema key `palette-app-state-v1`)
- Platform differences go behind conditional imports or an interface, never `kIsWeb` checks scattered in widgets

## Dependencies

- Prefer the Flutter/Dart SDK and first-party packages for simple tasks
- Before adding a package, check [pub.dev](https://pub.dev/) for the most popular, well-maintained option, and confirm it supports both Android and web
- Bundle fonts and assets; do not load them from a CDN at runtime

## Responsive Layout

- Choose layouts from available width with `LayoutBuilder`/`MediaQuery`, never from device type or platform
- Breakpoints: narrow < 600 dp (phone), medium 600–1023 dp (tablet), wide >= 1024 dp
- Never lock orientation; state must survive rotation, resize, and split-screen

## User Experience

- When the user must wait for async work, show a **loading indicator** (progress, skeleton, or shimmer); never block the UI thread: heavy work (k-means, image decode) runs in an isolate via `compute`
- Use **shimmer placeholders** for images that load slowly
- Provide feedback (SnackBar/toast) for copy, export, and errors

## Accessibility & Code Quality

- **Semantics:** add `Semantics`/`tooltip`/labels for non-text controls; support keyboard focus and screen readers
- **Touch targets:** at least 48x48 dp
- **WCAG color:** meet contrast ratios (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text); never rely on color alone to convey state
- **Clean code:** early returns, descriptive names, single-responsibility functions, `const` constructors where possible
- Run `flutter analyze` and `flutter test` before committing; both must pass
